{"type":"text","data":"432 into its binary representation:\n$8432 = 8192 + 12"}
{"type":"text","data":"8 + 64 + 32 + 16$ (which is $100000"}
{"type":"text","data":"11110000_2$).\n\nHere are the successive squaring steps for $7^k \\pmod"}
{"type":"text","data":"{5557}$:\n*   $7^1 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{5557}$\n*"}
{"type":"text","data":"   $7^2 \\equiv 49 \\pmod{5557}$\n*   $7^"}
{"type":"text","data":"4 \\equiv 49^2 = 2401 \\pmod{5557}$\n*   $7"}
{"type":"text","data":"^8 \\equiv 2401^2 = 5764801 \\equiv 2"}
